# Citation metadata, in Citation File Format. GitHub reads this and offers a
# "Cite this repository" button from it.
#
# The version and date below are stamped by packaging/stamp-docs.py along with
# the docs site, so a release cannot leave them behind. Do not edit them by hand.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: SidStation ASID
message: If you refer to this software, please cite it using this metadata.
type: software
abstract: >-
    A cross platform audio plugin (VST3, AU and Standalone) that plays the three
    SID voices of the Elektron SidStation hardware synthesiser from a DAW. It
    streams raw MOS6581 register writes over the ASID protocol rather than sending
    MIDI CC, so each voice gets its own pitch, gate and register control, one
    plugin instance per voice. It requires the hardware and contains no emulation.
authors:
    - family-names: Dehli
      given-names: Benjamin
      website: https://www.dehlimusikk.no/
repository-code: https://github.com/benjamindehli/sidstation-asid
url: https://benjamindehli.github.io/sidstation-asid/
license: GPL-3.0-only
version: 1.1.2
date-released: "2026-08-11"
keywords:
    - SidStation
    - Elektron
    - ASID
    - SID
    - MOS6581
    - chiptune
    - audio plugin
    - VST3
    - audio unit
    - JUCE
